{title: To God Be the Glory}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby}
{key: G}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune TO GOD BE THE GLORY - William H. Doane (1875)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1875, tune 1875: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
To [G]God be the glory, great [C]things He hath [G]done;
So loved He the world that He [A]gave us His [D]Son,
Who [G]yielded His life an a[C]tonement for [G]sin,
And [C]opened the [G]life gate that [D]all may go [G]in.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [G]earth hear His voice!
[D]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord, let the [G]people rejoice!
O [G]come to the Father, through [C]Jesus the [G]Son,
And [C]give Him the [G]glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done.
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O [G]perfect redemption, the [C]purchase of [G]blood,
To every believer the [A]promise of [D]God;
The [G]vilest offender who [C]truly be[G]lieves,
That [C]moment from [G]Jesus a [D]pardon re[G]ceives.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Great [G]things He hath taught us, great [C]things He hath [G]done,
And great our rejoicing through [A]Jesus the [D]Son;
But [G]purer, and higher, and [C]greater will [G]be
Our [C]wonder, our [G]transport, when [D]Jesus we [G]see.
{end_of_verse}
